.TH SDL_strlcpy 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_strlcpy \- Copy a string.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_strlcpy(char *dst, const char *src, size_t maxlen);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function copies up to
.BR maxlen
- 1 characters from
.BR src
to
.BR dst ,
then appends a null terminator\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR maxlen
is 0, no characters are copied and no null terminator is written\[char46]
.PP
If you want to copy an UTF-8 string but need to ensure that multi-byte sequences are not truncated, consider using
.BR SDL_utf8strlcpy ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I dst
The destination buffer\[char46] Must not be NULL, and must not overlap with
.BR src \[char46]

.TP
.I src
The null-terminated string to copy\[char46] Must not be NULL, and must not overlap with
.BR dst \[char46]

.TP
.I maxlen
The length (in characters) of the destination buffer\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the length (in characters, excluding the null terminator) of
.BR src \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_strlcat (3),
.BR SDL_utf8strlcpy (3)
